From 05411dd0c55f0d89590bc4524a4a69da3ac987a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@local>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 09:10:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use real OSRM road distance for route-finder totals/fare and
 route list/detail pages

- routing.py: attach OSRM foot-profile geometry to walking transfer
  legs (previously skipped entirely); sum real per-leg OSRM distance
  for the response's total_cost and fare lookup instead of the
  routing graph's haversine (straight-line) edge-weight sum, with a
  fallback to the old behavior if OSRM is unreachable for a leg.
- schemas.py: correct RouteAlternative docstring -- its total_cost is
  still haversine-based (alternatives skip OSRM by design), previously
  mislabeled as 'exact'.
- models/route.py + migration 9d3f1a7c2b4e: add nullable
  Route.osrm_distance_km.
- scripts/compute_osrm_route_distances.py: one-off/re-runnable script
  to batch-compute osrm_distance_km per route via OSRM, using the same
  waypoint-thinning as the live route-finder.
- frontend: lib/routeDistance.ts picks osrm_distance_km over
  approx_distance_km wherever available; wired into the routes list
  and route detail pages.
